# Root .dockerignore — docker-compose.yml builds backend/Dockerfile with a
# repo-root build context (needed so that Dockerfile can COPY protocol/,
# which schema_validation.py expects at /protocol/schemas — see that
# Dockerfile's COPY comment). Docker only reads .dockerignore from the
# BUILD CONTEXT ROOT, so this file — not backend/.dockerignore, which is
# now dead — is what actually protects secrets from being baked into an
# image layer. Without the block below, backend/.env (real secrets:
# JWT_SECRET, DATABASE_URL credentials, OPENROUTER_API_KEY, DEEPGRAM_API_KEY,
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY, TURN_SECRET) gets baked into an image layer the moment
# a developer follows .env.example's own instructions and creates it —
# recoverable from `docker history`/`docker save` even after a later layer,
# and permanently so if the image is ever pushed to a registry.

backend/.env
backend/.env.*
!backend/.env.example

backend/.venv/
backend/venv/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
backend/.pytest_cache/
backend/.mypy_cache/
backend/.ruff_cache/
backend/tests/

.git/
.github/
.claude/
android/
docs/
infra/
*.md
bash.exe.stackdump
